Refresh main/fakeroot distfile checksum.

salsa.debian.org regenerated the auto-generated tag archive for
upstream/1.37.1.2 (GitLab archives are not byte-stable across archive-code
upgrades), so the pinned sha256 no longer matches what the server serves.

Content verified before accepting the new hash (2026-07-17): the tarball
tree is byte-identical to a fresh `git clone --branch upstream/1.37.1.2`
of the same salsa repo, modulo .gitattributes/.gitignore which are
export-ignored from archives. Compression metadata is the only change.

Upstream cports master still carries the stale hash and will hit the same
failure on any cold fetch — upstreamable as-is (see UPSTREAMING.md).

